{"title":"2021 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is drawn outside of equilateral triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Regular hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b15a8079281095d74ac43e92d9eab3bb1b3080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEFGHI$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" /> is drawn outside of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />. If the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1bf55dee68ba4123ca736e3b4b2121ffebc98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AED$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is 3, then the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/61986fb9aca15a3d9fa47a37f10e6cc396e2ed1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AGH$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a710ff759753fcf79c3176e8d1e93eddefc2d7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\sqrt{b}-c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is a squarefree positive integer. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d1f49c6bd7aa2f64b76922bd518307e3da3611.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(300); import olympiad; real s = 1; pair B = (0,0); pair C = (s,0); pair A = (s/2,sqrt(3)/2*s); pair D = (s,-s); pair E = (0,-s); pair F = (-s/2,-s-sqrt(3)/2*s); pair G = (0,-s-sqrt(3)*s); pair H = (s,-s-sqrt(3)*s); pair I = (3*s/2,-s-sqrt(3)/2*s);  draw(A--B--C--cycle, black); draw(B--C--D--E--cycle, black); draw(D--E--F--G--H--I--cycle, black);  filldraw(A--E--D--cycle, lightblue+opacity(0.25), black+linewidth(0.8)); filldraw(A--G--H--cycle, lightgreen+opacity(0.22), black+linewidth(0.8));  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, NW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, NW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;, G, S); label(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, S); label(&quot;$I$&quot;, I, NE);  draw(E--D, dashed+gray); draw(G--H, dashed+gray); [/asy]\" width=\"295\" height=\"502\" /> </center><p> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a4388c3b0389ad9b07d053d845004af520090c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Firstly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a324e0f2c1a06275733b28bd0550c3ace7f28c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED=GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> since both are sides of a regular hexagon. Now, the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2afec04e3636c80fa3d89e5468045595151c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/1563dc46ab3b223385ee5711582232b3b54eb268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+1\\right) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"185\" height=\"55\" /> and the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc2afec04e3636c80fa3d89e5468045595151c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ED$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/1/bd1d51518c1deddfab72de999c6adca0fbb12b4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+1+\\sqrt{3}\\right) = \\frac{2+3\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"240\" height=\"55\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac9cd75e01c06a5a6c4299e38e669114f788a668.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[AGH]=\\frac{\\frac{2+3\\sqrt{3}}{2}}{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2}}[AED]=(4\\sqrt{3}-5)(3)=12\\sqrt{3}-15\\implies12+3+15=\\boxed{30}.\\]\" width=\"577\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017043653\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 80/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4136/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26402:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017043653 and revision id 274611. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}